  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Who owns the counters and budget?",
      "items": [
        "pRetry initializes and increments attemptNumber; it increments retriesConsumed only after onAttemptFailure returns true.",
        "maxRetryTime is measured from pRetry's startTime. Infinity means no retry-time cap; it is not a deadline imposed on a running input operation."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Failed attempt: exact decision order",
      "items": [
        "AbortError is unwrapped first. With time remaining, shouldConsumeRetry runs, then onFailedAttempt runs, then time/retries and non-network TypeError guards run before shouldRetry.",
        "A false consume decision can still retry after shouldRetry approves, but it neither consumes a retry nor waits."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Where cancellation reaches",
      "items": [
        "AbortSignal stops entry checks and rejects a pending delay by clearing its timeout; it is checked again after waiting.",
        "pRetry calls input only with attemptNumber, so aborting its signal does not itself cancel an already-running caller operation."
      ]
    }
  ]
